      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "NOTE",
      "pageStart": 5,
      "pageEnd": 6,
      "target": "../sections/sec-011-note.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The ODRL Information Model provides a logical view of the components of the Policy model. The implementable view of\nthe ODRL Information Model is provided by various encoding serialisations as normatively described in the ODRL\nVocabulary & Expression document [odrl-vocab]. The mapping of the logical Information Model components to the\nimplementable serialisations may require some trade-offs and/or differences depending on the features supported by the\nserialisation language.\nIn the latter case, the profile property MUST be used to indicate the IRIs of the ODRL Profile(s). See the ODRL Profiles",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
