      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Relation Property",
      "pageStart": 8,
      "pageEnd": 9,
      "target": "../sections/sec-018-221-relation-property.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The abstract relation property is used to create an explicit link between an Action and an Asset, indicating how the Asset MUST\nbe utilised in respect to the Rule that links to it.\nAn ODRL validator MUST support the following sub-properties of relation:\ntarget: indicates that the Asset is the primary subject to which the Rule action directly applies.\nAdditional relation subtype properties MAY be defined in the ODRL Common Vocabulary [odrl-vocab] and ODRL Profiles.\nExample Use Case: The assigner Party http//example.com/party:0001 offers to display the target Asset\nhttp://example.com/asset:3333.",
