      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "ODRL Profiles",
      "pageStart": 29,
      "pageEnd": 30,
      "target": "../sections/sec-050-3-odrl-profiles.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The Conflict Strategy requirements include:\n1. If a Policy has the conflict property of perm then any conflicting Permission Rule MUST override the Prohibition Rule.\n2. If a Policy has the conflict property of prohibit then any conflicting Prohibition Rule MUST override the Permission\nRule.\n3. If a Policy has the conflict property of invalid then any conflicting Rules MUST void the entire Policy.\n4. If a Policy has multiple conflict property values (for example, after a Policy merge or inheritance) and there are\nconflicting Rules then the entire Policy MUST be void.\nExample Use Case: Two Polic",
      "truncated": true,
